<title>NORWAY: TABLE-Kvaerner H1 pre-tax up 19 pct.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Kvaerner H1 pre-tax up 19 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30.</p>
<p>				  (millions of crowns unless stated)</p>
<p>   Operating revenues	   33,089	vs	  22,942</p>
<p>   Operating profit		  963	vs	     558</p>
<p>   Pre-tax profit		    840	vs	     706</p>
<p>   Net profit			  605	vs	     515</p>
<p>   EPS H1  (crowns)		13.89	vs	   11.86</p>
<p>NOTE -- Full name of Anglo-Norwegian construction and engineering company is Kvaerner ASA. Kvaerner acquired British conglomerate Trafalgar House Plc in April, 1996. Comparative H1 figures include two months from operations of Trafalgar House.</p>
<p>Ten Norwegian and international analysts forecast a first-half operating result of 1.20 billion crowns and pre-tax profits of 1.01 billion crowns.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
